# Amendment #84 — M3 wire per-component CLIs as [project.scripts] console-script entries

2026-04-29. Multi-component sealed amendment for the OSS v0.1.0
publish programme. M3 per locked programme master plan-doc
`docs/rebuild/plans/oss-v0-1-0-publish.md` §5 M3 row + §6
sequencing rule #3 + §3 AC.OSS.2 (D-3 — per-component CLIs are
authored but unregistered). Sub-plan-doc:
`docs/rebuild/plans/oss-v0-1-0-publish-wire-clis.md`.

Composes on the M1.rename multi-amendment series (sealed M1a..M1g
2026-04-29; M1g seal `f6c22fd`; §14 backfill `d5b8dcd`) and on
M2.partition (sealed `4cda805` 2026-04-29; §14 backfill `bb3574c`).

M3 closes the AC.OSS.2 D-3 gap surfaced by the feature-usage
audit (`.scratch/claude-output/feature-usage-audit.md` §D-3 line
430): per-component CLIs (`loam.safety_layer.cli`,
`loam.cost_governance.cli`, `loam.self_correction.cli`,
`loam.reversibility_primitive.cli`) ship working argparse
parsers but no `[project.scripts]` registrations expose them.
Operators who type `loam-kill scope <id>` (etc.) get
`command not found`.

M3 registers five console-scripts across four pyproject.toml
files:

  framework/safety-layer/pyproject.toml:
    loam-kill = "loam.safety_layer.cli:main"

  framework/cost-governance/pyproject.toml:
    loam-cost = "loam.cost_governance.cli:main"

  framework/self-correction/pyproject.toml:
    loam-correction = "loam.self_correction.cli:main"

  framework/reversibility-primitive/pyproject.toml:
    loam-reversibility = "loam.reversibility_primitive.cli:main_reversibility"
    loam-rollback = "loam.reversibility_primitive.cli:main_rollback"

Three of the four existing `cli.main` callables are zero-arg
entry-point compatible. The fourth — `loam.reversibility_primitive.cli.main`
— has signature `main(call: CliCall, argv: list[str] | None = None)`
requiring a positional `CliCall` arg (the docstring at line 12-13
notes "production wiring is a thin wrapper in the workspace
bootstrap" — but no such wrapper is shipped). M3 adds two NEW
public shim functions `main_reversibility(argv)` and
`main_rollback(argv)` to that module, each:

  1. Builds its own argparse parser exposing only its respective
     subtree (`reversibility {bind, handlers}` for `main_reversibility`;
     `rollback {scope, status}` for `main_rollback`).
  2. Reads `--socket` / `POS_SOCKET_PATH` to resolve the
     orchestrator IPC socket (mirrors `loam.safety_layer.cli`
     pattern verbatim; verified at plan-authoring time that
     M1b did NOT rename `POS_SOCKET_PATH`, so the env-var name
     stays consistent across kill/safety + reversibility/rollback
     CLIs per plan §10 D-build.M3.2).
  3. Builds an `IPCClient`, connects, wraps `client.call` as a
     `CliCall` lambda.
  4. Calls the existing `dispatch(call, args)` function with
     resolved args; the per-shim parser sets `args.cmd` to the
     constant `"reversibility"` or `"rollback"` so the existing
     dispatch function dispatches correctly without modification.

Existing `main(call, argv)` + `build_parser` + `dispatch` preserved
untouched per dispatch constraint "no change to the `main()`
function itself" — the design is additive (NEW shim functions
around an unchanged `main`). Any future workspace-bootstrap
wrapper that injects a `CliCall` directly remains supported.

Naming convention: `loam-*` per master plan §5 M3 row + post-M1g
rebranded identity. Deviates from feature-usage-audit's in-text
`pos-*` suggestion (audit pre-dates M1g; master plan + dispatch
authoritative per plan §10 D-build.M3.5). The five existing
`pos-*` binaries (`pos-obs` + `pos-bootstrap` + `pos-sync` +
`pos-workspace-sync` + `pos`) STAY on the `pos-*` prefix per
M1g's FIDRAFT-deferral ruling — those are out of M3's named
scope.

Editable-install refresh: `pip install -e framework/<comp>/`
re-run for each of the four touched components inside the shared
venv `<repo>/.venv/` so the new `loam-*` binaries become bootable
from PATH. The registration test (post-build) reads
`importlib.metadata.entry_points(group="console_scripts")` —
entry-point metadata refreshes automatically from `pip install -e`.

Tests: 4 new test files (one per component; reversibility-primitive's
covers both entries) — each asserts the corresponding `loam-*`
entry-point is registered + dispatches to the expected callable
via `importlib.metadata.entry_points`. Test scope deliberately
narrow per dispatch constraint — registration is the AC, not
behaviour. No actual shell invocation.

Sealed-component fence: 4 components (safety-layer, cost-governance,
self-correction, reversibility-primitive). HOL narrative-target
only — HOL is not in `components:` because M3 doesn't bump HOL's
sidecar; HOL hosts this narrative file by convention per M1c..M2
precedent. The structural fences are the four component subtrees:

  framework/safety-layer/
  framework/cost-governance/
  framework/self-correction/
  framework/reversibility-primitive/

Each fence's diff is intentionally minimal: a single `[project.scripts]`
block in pyproject.toml + a single new test file (plus, for
reversibility-primitive, two new shim functions in cli.py).

